  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1122 PM CDT Sat Jun 6 2026\n\nA 500mb ridge across across northwest Texas Monday night will \nslowly shift eastward Tuesday into Tues night. This will provide \nsubsidence across west central Texas Mon night through the rest of\nthe week as the upper level ridge of high pressure elongates and \nprevails across northeast Mexico and Texas through Friday. Near \nnormal high temperatures Monday and Tuesday will become above \nnormal on Wednesday and remain above normal through the rest of \nthe week into the weekend. The 500mb ridge is expected to shift \nwestward towards the weekend as a 500mb trough develops and \ndeepens across the east-central portions of  the United States \nSaturday into Sunday. This will allow some convection to develop \nacross northern portions of the CWA Sat night into Sunday. \nOtherwise...not much in the way of rain chances are expected \nthrough the long term.",
